<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Harlaw</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1411">1411</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Harlaw was fought on 24 July 1411 near Inverurie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aberdeenshire">Aberdeenshire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donald-lord-of-the-isles">Donald, Lord of the Isles</a>, pressing his wife's claim to the earldom of Ross, led a Highland army against forces raised by Alexander Stewart, Earl of Mar. The battle was bloody but indecisive; Donald withdrew to the west, and it was long remembered as a clash between Highland and Lowland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-harlaw.jpg" alt="Battle of Harlaw" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrew Wood · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bennachie_from_the_east.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
